 "description": "<p>HBG2 at&nbsp;66&deg;50 N -&nbsp;54&deg;42 W&nbsp;is a standard hydrographic station&nbsp;on the Sisimiut section and&nbsp;part of the Greenland Institute of Natural Resources monitoring program. The purpose of the marine monitoring program is to register specific&nbsp;physical properties&nbsp;of the sea water column,&nbsp;such as temperature and&nbsp;salinity,&nbsp;at the same geographical location&nbsp;once every year, and compare these repeated registrations&nbsp;with&nbsp;previous years&#39; recordings. Hydrographic measurements are&nbsp;typical carried out with a so-called &quot;CTD&quot; instrument (Conductivity, Temperature, and Depth). The hydrographic station is&nbsp;monitored one time each year&nbsp;in June/July.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 20.2500019073486px; line-height: 24.3000011444092px;\">.</span></p>",
